# Felkyo Creatures — Git LFS (Large File Storage) configuration.
#
# WHAT THIS IS FOR: our creatures are delivered as animated GIFs, and the site
# uses larger pieces of art (backgrounds, decorative frames). These are binary
# files that change as whole blobs. Storing them directly in Git would bloat the
# repository history and make every clone slow. Git LFS keeps a tiny text pointer
# in Git and stores the real bytes separately, so the repo stays small.
#
# HOW IT WORKS: any path matched below is stored via LFS instead of normal Git.
# You need Git LFS installed once per machine ("git lfs install"); the setup
# guide in docs/ explains this.
#
# HOW TO ADD MORE: if a new kind of art folder appears, add a matching line here
# following the same pattern.

# All art living under these two folders goes to LFS, whatever its extension.
public/assets/creatures/**  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
public/assets/art/**        filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Belt-and-braces: these image/source formats go to LFS wherever they appear,
# so a stray large asset outside the folders above is still stored efficiently.
*.gif   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.apng  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.webp  filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
*.psd   filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# Keep line endings sane across Windows and the Linux production host:
# text files are normalised to LF in the repository.
* text=auto eol=lf
